@inherits LayoutComponentBase

<PageTitle>The Realm</PageTitle>

@* The shell is the outermost element and the five providers sit inside it (03 section 3.2 as amended by D67, CR2-001). A MudBlazor popover or
   dialog renders its content inside its own provider, and Blazor resolves a cascading parameter by walking up from the component that renders the
   fragment, so a value reaches the sheet and every dialog only if the provider is below the cascade. The shell renders no element.

   The DOM order is the Tab order (01 section 10.2, R1-15, [AC-47]): the page first (on Location: attribution, bubbles, right stack, map canvas), then
   MudPopoverProvider, which is where the sheet lives (handle, section tabs, content), then the nav (Location, Driving, Settings). The provider has to come after the page and before the nav, and the other
   providers draw nothing in the page until a dialog or a snackbar is open, so their place is free. Stacking is by z-index, never by DOM order. *@
<RealmShell>
    <MudThemeProvider Theme="Realm.Web.Theme.RealmTheme.Create()" IsDarkMode="true" ObserveSystemDarkModeChange="false" />
    <MudDialogProvider />
    <MudSnackbarProvider />
    <MudXProvider />

    <ConnectionBanner />

    <main id="realm-main" aria-label="The Realm">
        @Body
    </main>

    <MudPopoverProvider />
    <BottomNav />
</RealmShell>
